  "summary": "Chapter 9, Smooth Monge--Ampere equations, receives a complete recursive reader revision. Four connected opening paragraphs explain the jointly unknown potential and normalization scalar, the weighted potential bound and trace ellipticity, adjoint compatibility, proper exponential solvability, scalar variations and Hopf normalization. The separate Gauduchon-volume deformation retains the initial-metric condition for preserving an Aeppli class and limits uniqueness to its scalar ansatz. The closing transition to Chapter 10 explicitly requires nonnegative, nonzero Lp densities with p>1. All statements, proofs and original problem scopes remain unchanged. The final 1666-line chapter, including 11 inputs and 30 proofs, is read completely twice; its complete output and both dated covers are inspected. The 1758-page release and matching homepage are live at the verified public commit.",
